# LWS 1.0 storage description resource -- minimal ShExC shape.
#
# RDF counterpart of schema/json/storage-description.json, derived from the
# LWS 1.0 core specification (lws10-core/Discovery.html, § storage
# description data model / representation). Published under
# https://w3id.org/lws/test/shape/storage-description; the harness serves
# this local copy under that IRI (see context.ts).
#
# Data model mapped to RDF:
#   JSON                       RDF
#   id (REQUIRED, URI)         the focus node is an IRI (<storage-description> IRI)
#   type === Storage           a lws:Storage (canonical single-type form)
#   service (REQUIRED)         did:service, one triple per service
#     type === StorageRoot     a lws:StorageRoot for the mandatory root service
#     serviceEndpoint (REQ)    did:serviceEndpoint IRI
#   capability (OPTIONAL)      lws:capability, one triple per capability
#     type (REQUIRED)          a <type>
#
#   Service and capability types are required in RDF too. The suite's served
#   LWS context post-patches missing service terms once they are not yet in
#   the upstream vocabulary (TypeIndexService, TypeSearchService; see
#   scripts/generate-lws-v1-context.ts), so those types survive JSON-LD
#   expansion. A type the patched vocab still does not know is dropped in
#   conversion, and only the JSON schema can check it.
#
# Notes on expressiveness (documented gaps vs the JSON schema):
#   - "type equals X or a set containing X": ShEx value sets have subset
#     semantics, so a set like ["Storage", ...] fails; these shapes match
#     the canonical single-type form the spec examples and current
#     implementations emit.
#   - service/capability "id" (a URI if present) has no RDF triple -- the
#     id IS the node -- so it is not checked; a service or capability with
#     an id is simply an IRI node instead of a blank node.
#   - required-at-least-one StorageRoot service is expressed as exactly one
#     did:service @<StorageRootService> plus any number of @<Service> --
#     shex.js consumes one service as the base StorageRoot service and the
#     rest as generic services (order-insensitive).
PREFIX lws: <https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#>
PREFIX did: <https://www.w3.org/ns/did#>

start = @<storage-description>

<storage-description> IRI {
  a [ lws:Storage ] ;
  did:service @<StorageRootService> ;
  did:service @<Service>* ;
  lws:capability @<Capability>* ;
}

<StorageRootService> {
  a [ lws:StorageRoot ] ;
  did:serviceEndpoint IRI ;
}

<Service> {
  a .+ ;
  did:serviceEndpoint IRI ;
}

<Capability> {
  a .+ ;
}